- Independent algebra: `_tmp_kimi_b6_sympy.py`, 13 checks, output `ALL_PASS` (SymPy 1.14.0, /usr/bin/python3).
- Lane files read in full (contents, not names): B6 target, B1_RESULT_V2, B1_SCOPE_QUALIFICATION, B3_CLASS_FILED, B3_RESCUE, BOUNCE_ROUTE_SUMMARY.

## 9. Uncertainties and what I did not inspect

- Claims bind to the saved publisher bytes whose SHA matches B6's pin; I did not re-fetch Springer live (lane records note a cookie handshake). If the saved file diverges from the live version of record, both B6 and this review inherit that; I found no internal sign of divergence (metadata, equation numbering, and section structure are all coherent).
- I verified printed Eq. (28) from printed (11) rather than re-deriving the KS Einstein tensor from the metric; (11) is the printed matter-independent combination, which suffices for the shear law.
- Printed Eq. (31) (Raychaudhuri) is quoted by B6 but is not load-bearing for either verdict; I did not check its external sign conventions.
- The arXiv copy in the lane was not used and was not needed; per the rules, no claim here rests on it.
- Constraint compliance: report only — I modified no lane artifact; my only writes are the `_tmp_*` scripts/dumps listed above and this report.

