+Closure (c) independently gives (t_b=0.31398069180858207), (e_b=4150.244522227945) and (\dot H_b=1316.4810148631486). The two coordinate formulations agree; their independently measured constraint errors are reported separately below. To reconstruct the full representative (c) row, its regular (F) branch must cover approximately (e\in[1.1,4150.24452223]), with a neighbourhood for the continuation. No such broad temperature-domain assumption is needed for the local existence proof.
